{"source": "zap-event", "timestamp": "2026-04-02T11:26:47.911315Z", "ip": "192.168.50.77", "port": "80", "alert": "Missing Anti-clickjacking Header", "alert_desc": "The response does not protect against 'ClickJacking' attacks. It should include either Content-Security-Policy with 'frame-ancestors' directive or X-Frame-Options.", "risk": "2", "confidence": "2", "url": "http://192.168.50.77", "request_header": "GET http://192.168.50.77 HTTP/1.1\r\nhost: 192.168.50.77\r\nuser-agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/141.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\r\npragma: no-cache\r\ncache-control: no-cache\r\nCookie: PHPSESSID=pdmuq8h16e56ccd30is9b19k90; security=low\r\n\r\n", "solution": "Modern Web browsers support the Content-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options HTTP headers. Ensure one of them is set on all web pages returned by your site/app.If you expect the page to be framed only by pages on your server (e.g. it's part of a FRAMESET) then you'll want to use SAMEORIGIN, otherwise if you never expect the page to be framed, you should use DENY. Alternatively consider implementing Content Security Policy's \"frame-ancestors\" directive.", "solution_reference": "<p>https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/X-Frame-Options</p>"}
